A||N||3||londerville||couple questions||||1||
Z||000000||londerville||09-10-2001||04:17 AM||||Hi,<BR>How hard is it to install power windows and locks in a car that does not have them?<P>Also, how much do GT front bumpers usually cost?<P>Thanx<BR>Jason||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||09-10-2001||07:42 AM||||If I remember correctly from reading past posts, it's much easier to replace the entire door than to install power windows in your doors.  Try searching "Technical Discussions" for more detail.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||09-10-2001||08:33 AM||||Whether you replace the entire door or just the guts you'll still need the wiring harness, switches, power lock relay, and fuses.  Cars not originally equipped with power windows and locks do not have the wiring installed for them.  It is a separate harness altogether.  You can get one from a donor car or make your own.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||09-10-2001||09:12 AM||||Here's a link to a writeup about adding PW/PL.  The link at the top of the page will get you to a pdf file that also has some drawings.<P>If you can find a bumper at a u-pull-it, you may pay $20-$30.  The Fiero Store has them for $386.  You can pay anywhere in that range.....||||reg||1
